From: OCCTSwift ecosystem <noreply@secondmouse.au>
Subject: [PATCH] Data Exchange - split oversized raw STEP strings in
 StepData_StepWriter::AddString instead of looping forever

**Backports [Open-Cascade-SAS/OCCT#1318](https://github.com/Open-Cascade-SAS/OCCT/pull/1318)** (open,
by an OCCT maintainer, pinned to commit `72bc2368372d93d6f84717f2327131d4c000d7c1`). No linked
upstream issue; the PR description states the fix directly. Audited and queued in
[#323](https://github.com/SecondMouseAU/OCCTSwift/issues/323).

`StepData_StepWriter::AddString` writes a raw token into the writer's current-line buffer
(`thecurr`, fixed at `StepLong` = 72 characters), flushing the buffered line to `thefile` and
resetting it whenever the pending text won't fit:

```cpp
while (!thecurr.CanGet(lnstr + more))
{
  thefile->Append(thecurr.Moved());
  ...
  thecurr.SetInitial(indst);
}
thecurr.Add(astr, lnstr);
```

This assumes the token itself is never longer than one full line. When `lnstr + more` exceeds
`StepLong` — a single unbroken string value (e.g. a long name/label field with no natural break
point) longer than 72 characters — `thecurr.CanGet(lnstr + more)` is **never** true no matter how
many times the line is flushed and reset: the loop runs forever. Same subsystem as patch `0002`.

**Fix:** when the token fits within `StepLong`, behavior is unchanged (flush-then-add). When it
doesn't, the new code splits the token across as many lines as needed — filling each line with as
much of the token as fits, flushing, and continuing with the remainder — instead of looping on a
single `CanGet` check that can never become true. Continuation lines also drop their indentation
when the indented prefix would leave no room for the pending text.

**Validation** (fast path, no full rebuild — see the `#0001` entry above for the override-link
technique): `StepData_StepWriter::StartEntity` + `SendString` (the public entry point; `AddString`
itself is private) with a 200-character unbroken string hangs indefinitely on stock p1 (confirmed by
wall-clock timeout) and returns instantly after the patch, correctly split across three continuation
lines with the original text intact end-to-end. A separate sanity check with only normal-length
string/int fields produces **byte-identical** `Print()` output before and after the patch.

**Retire** once the bundled OCCT includes this fix (open PR — pin to the SHA above and re-verify if
it changes in review).
---
 src/DataExchange/TKDESTEP/StepData/StepData_StepWriter.cxx | 55 ++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 40 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/DataExchange/TKDESTEP/StepData/StepData_StepWriter.cxx b/src/DataExchange/TKDESTEP/StepData/StepData_StepWriter.cxx
index cb8fb7fb..bcc2dd99 100644
--- a/src/DataExchange/TKDESTEP/StepData/StepData_StepWriter.cxx
+++ b/src/DataExchange/TKDESTEP/StepData/StepData_StepWriter.cxx
@@ -1221,34 +1221,59 @@ void StepData_StepWriter::EndEntity()
 
 void StepData_StepWriter::AddString(const TCollection_AsciiString& astr, const int more)
 {
-  while (!thecurr.CanGet(astr.Length() + more))
-  {
-    thefile->Append(thecurr.Moved());
-    int indst = thelevel * 2;
-    if (theindent)
-    {
-      indst += theindval;
-    }
-    thecurr.SetInitial(indst);
-  }
-  thecurr.Add(astr);
+  AddString(astr.ToCString(), astr.Length(), more);
 }
 
 //=================================================================================================
 
 void StepData_StepWriter::AddString(const char* const astr, const int lnstr, const int more)
 {
-  while (!thecurr.CanGet(lnstr + more))
-  {
+  const auto flushLine = [this](const int theRequired) {
     thefile->Append(thecurr.Moved());
     int indst = thelevel * 2;
     if (theindent)
     {
       indst += theindval;
     }
-    thecurr.SetInitial(indst);
+    thecurr.SetInitial(indst < StepLong && indst + theRequired <= StepLong ? indst : 0);
+  };
+
+  if (lnstr + more <= StepLong)
+  {
+    while (!thecurr.CanGet(lnstr + more))
+    {
+      flushLine(lnstr + more);
+    }
+    thecurr.Add(astr, lnstr);
+    return;
+  }
+
+  int aStart = 0;
+  int aRest  = lnstr;
+  while (aRest > 0)
+  {
+    if (thecurr.CanGet(aRest + more))
+    {
+      thecurr.Add(astr + aStart, aRest);
+      return;
+    }
+
+    const int aRoom = StepLong - thecurr.Length();
+    if (aRoom <= 0 || (aRest + more <= StepLong && aRoom < aRest + more))
+    {
+      flushLine(aRest + more <= StepLong ? aRest + more : 0);
+      continue;
+    }
+
+    const int aChunk = (aRest < aRoom ? aRest : aRoom);
+    thecurr.Add(astr + aStart, aChunk);
+    aStart += aChunk;
+    aRest -= aChunk;
+    if (aRest > 0)
+    {
+      flushLine(aRest + more <= StepLong ? aRest + more : 0);
+    }
   }
-  thecurr.Add(astr, lnstr);
 }
 
 //   FINAL SENDING
